    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In the UK, the inheritance tax (IHT) laws apply to the assets held by the grantor ((not the trust) when it passes away), regardless of the ownership structure. The only way trust assets are taxed is if the assets are drawn on, effectively transferring them from the trust to the individual. Offshore accounts are generally not subject to IHT in the UK, but such is rarely permitted meaning that accounts in some countries may be considered \"exempt\" but be subject to double taxation or simply none taxed.",
